  (text "Matrix Link:\nUsed to connect the Xn keys to the\nMAIN matrix when used on single\nmatrix systems. Creates 8x9 Matrix.\n\n* For std CLCD keyboard, Jumper J4 only.\n* For 8x9 matrix, jumper J3 only."
    (at 294.005 231.14 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5494 1.5494)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 8cd43328-f436-48cd-9edb-3044181084e3)
  )
  (text "Commodore LCD prototype (aka \"CLCD\") MX Keyboard\n\n- This keyboard is different from other CBM keyboards in that the special\n  control keys are not part of the main matrix, but are decoded separately.\n\nChanges from real CLCD Keyboard:\n\n- 6U spacebar with stabilizers.\n- Inverted T cursor keys using MX switches.\n- Relocated STOP key.\n- Re-sized Left SHIFT key.\n- Option to link special keys to main matrix, creating an 8x9 matrix.\n"
    (at 16.51 257.175 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5494 1.5494)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 9bac9ad3-a7b9-47f0-87c7-d8630653df68)
  )
  (text "CONNECTOR" (at 360.68 189.865 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.9972 2.9972) (thickness 0.5994) bold) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid af347946-e3da-4427-87ab-77b747929f50)
  )
  (text "CLCD-V2-R1 (Inverted T Cursor)" (at 317.5 267.335 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.9972 2.9972) (thickness 0.5994) bold) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid b6cd701f-4223-4e72-a305-466869ccb250)
